{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791790917,"nonce":"pMR6LNjx7PtxRy2lAHpc3rl5Bfg=","message":"Root cause isolated. HashLink's Haxe standard library implements haxe.io.Bytes.getData() as `new haxe.io.BytesData(b, length)`. BytesData's `@:to` conversion to hl.Bytes checks whether the new wrapper is null before reading its `bytes` field. After inlining, AIR still had a CondJump(NotNull) on the fresh object. SROA treated that branch use as an escape and retained one wrapper allocation per call.\n\nWorking-tree fix: an O3 pass after inlining folds null branches on provably non-null values and prunes the dead arm before SROA. In the optimized AIR for the reproducer's getter loop, the New/FieldSet/FieldGet wrapper sequence is gone and MemSet uses the original byte pointer. Added TestBytesDataAlloc with pointer identity, aliasing, copy, null-access, and exact zero-allocation checks.\n\nThe committed ChimpMonk reproducer measured 262064 bytes across 8192 getData calls before the fix and 0 after it with ASH_GC_TLAB=0. Cached writes and blits remained at 0. Verified on a fresh Ash release build in pinned Cranelift, pinned LLVM, and default hybrid; the Ash regression also passes in interpreter and Cranelift hot-reload modes. All 205 AIR unit tests pass. LLVM with --hot-reload still allocates 786352 bytes in this fixture because that mode does not inline the wrapper; this change does not touch dispatch and the issue's hot-reload requirement was conditional on a dispatch change.\n\nIssue remains open until the working-tree fix is committed.","files":null}]}